From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0422-mem-join-01.patch

Source: 0422-mem-join-01.patch
Core patch, Lichii PR 288 (zortos293/Lichii, open) behind a switch, off unless asked for. Applies on
the T28 core (t27core, through 0413) and on T30's patch list as 0419: preflight --fast lists the
same anchors as before.

JoinImages uploads a new image from guest memory, then runs the alias copies on top of it, oldest
first. When one of those copies writes every texel of the new image (a plain copy, same format and
ASTC opacity, neither image unwritten sparse, every level and layer from the origin, and only a copy
the loop would make: IsSafeGpuCopy, same sample count), the upload and the copies before it would
be overwritten whole, so they are not made. What RefreshContents does besides the upload still
happens: CpuModified cleared, the image tracked, its layout transitioned. The image comes out the
same.

Why it matters here: Ocarina of Time resizes a shadow map every frame in parts of Kokiri Forest at
one address (sizes about 780 to 1310 px); each size is a new depth target and a new texture, both
copied from older sizes and both uploaded first (4 to 7 MiB each). PR 288's run skipped about 700
uploads, 2.3 GB, and 5100 alias copies in 36 s; 54-57 fps became 58-60 on an RTX 4090. On the
console the uploads go through the stream ring and staging buffers that run 101 refused 25 times:
fewer uploads is less staging held and less GPU back-thread time. It does not lower what the pool
holds; that is a guess until the EDEN_REFUSED_STAGING and fps lines of a run say so. With the
switch unset the loop is the old one.

The log says "Upload skipped: a join copy writes the whole image (n so far)" every 500 skips.
Syntax-checked: vk_texture_cache.cpp and vk_rasterizer.cpp with the patched header, clang
-std=c++20 -fsyntax-only, against the T28 core with the port's boost, Vulkan and VMA headers.
Not built, not run.

